  "section": {
    "heading": "## User library — A new account confirms its email before the product opens",
    "text": "- A new account confirms its email by the link mailed to it before the product opens; until then it sees where the link was sent and can ask for another, start over with a different address, or log out.",
    "smoke": [
      "- Sign up with a new address: you see Confirm your email, and every other address of the app shows that same screen.",
      "- Tap the button in the mail: the app opens."
    ]
  },
  "notes": "The mandatory email confirmation, the library's part, on top of feat/sign-up-the-page-the-check-and-the-list. It binds only where a product registers DefaultEmailConfirmationConfigFactory (user-server EmailConfirmation); with none registered the library behaves as before. A product words the mail through DefaultEmailConfirmationLinkEmailConfigFactory. The page is user-ui pages/ConfirmEmail at account/verify-email; AuthenticatedPageContainer sends a waiting session there. The dev log-in's accounts are confirmed. Held: nothing landed or published. This library is published first and alone, then the app's branch of the same name."
